  (text
    "SLOT 1: generic M.2 3052/3042 Key-B WWAN socket. Pins checked vs Sierra EM92XX PTS Rev 5 (Jan 2025) + Telit FN990 HDG Rev 3.\nPCIe Gen3 x1 to switch port 1 (lane1); USB2 + USB3 to USB5744 port 1. Module TX AC caps on module.\nFULL_CARD_POWER_OFF# (pin 6): TCA6416A 3.3V push-pull + 47k PD (EM92 VIH 1.35-4.4V; FN990 1.8V/VPH domain, 47k internal PD) -> module off by default.\n  Firmware: drive FCPO# LOW before removing +3V7 (no high levels into an unpowered card - FN990 HDG 6.2.1 back-power note).\nRESET# (pin 67) and W_DISABLE1# (pin 8): open-drain 2N7002 only (both vendors forbid pull-up/push-pull on RESET#). Pulse >=1s covers EM92 (450ms) + FN990 (1s).\nPERST# = PCIE_PERST_N AND S_PCIE_EN_L (SN74LVC1G08, 3.3V; EM92 VIH 1.5V..VCC, FN990 VPH domain). 10k PD (rev 0.3, was PU) keeps PERST# low until\n  firmware sets PCIE_EN >=150ms after the slot rail is valid (EM92 T_pvpgl; no host signal into the card for the first 100ms). JP = hard PERST# hold.\nPin 20 host-IF select: NFET pulls pin 20 LOW while SLOTn_PCIE_SEL is HIGH (10k PU = default PCIe). Own expander line (U802 ex-spare), NOT PCIE_EN:\n  pin 20 is sampled at boot, while PERST# must stay gated low until >=150ms after power valid (EM92 T_pvpgl) - one line cannot do both.\n  FN990 USB_PCIE_SWITCH (int. 10k PU to 1.8V): LOW = PCIe (+USB debug), HIGH = USB only. EM92 PCIE_DIS (PD, max 2.1V): LOW/open = PCIe, HIGH = USB\n  -> fit the DNP 10k to +1V8 only to let PCIE_SEL=0 select USB on a Sierra card. Changing mode needs a module power cycle.\nPin 22: EM92 VBUS_SENSE (PD, 1.6-5.25V = USB present) / FN990 TGPIO_06 (1.8V). DNP 10k to slot rail: FIT ONLY for Sierra; NEVER with Telit.\nPin 28: EM92 PLA_S2_N (power-loss ack, LOW = safe to remove power) / FN990 TGPIO_08 -> test point (1.8V; not level-shifted in rev 0.3).\nPins 24/38/68 NC (EM92 optional VCC; FN990 TGPIO). Pin 73 = GND (both vendors) -> 3.3V sideband. 40-48 (UIM2), 56/58, 59-65, 23, 25, 26, CONFIG_x: NC.\nSIM: CUI NSIM-2-C card-detect closes to GND when card present. FN990 UIM1_PRESENT: active-low OK. EM92 SIM1_DETECT default 0V=absent: set polarity by AT\n  (configurable per PTS Table 2-1 note e) or disable hot-swap detect. ESD + 22pF filters near holder.\nGNSS / NTN antennas: NO carrier RF or GNSS bias circuit. All antennas are off-board pigtails on the card U.FL/MHF4 ports (see docs/antenna-gnss-plan.md).\n  FN990: internal GNSS bias LDO (2.9-3.15V, 100mA) on its GNSS port - active antenna OK. EM9291: GNSS on shared ANT1 - DC on ANT0-3 damages it: PASSIVE only.\nMechanical: standoff holes for 3052 (52mm) and 3042 (42mm) cards."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20.32 300 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "d45c1eb4-746a-5c52-b13c-216248578f9d"))
